{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788201243,"nonce":"CDiGFUnX3DW9Q2sm4Qg5S4QX4sQ=","title":"designate verbs report already-designated as not-designatable, so a redundant order is indistinguishable from an impossible one","message":"Found by W2 (autorimmer-41) while vetting 4087644, session 9, and routed out\nbecause it is outside that issue's territory. The analysis is confirmed against\nthe decompiled 1.6 source; the hazards below were read, not inferred.\n\n## The bug\n\n`Designator_Mine.CanDesignateCell` and `CanDesignateThing` return\n`AcceptanceReport.WasRejected` — which is `new AcceptanceReport(\"\")`, an EMPTY\nreason — for a cell that is already designated. `Designator_Hunt\n.CanDesignateThing` returns a bare `false`.\n\n`DesignateEngine.ReasonOf` correctly refuses to invent a reason it was not\ngiven, so it emits `{why:\"not-designatable\", reason:null}`. That envelope is\nindistinguishable from \"this rock is not mineable\" or \"this animal is not\nhuntable\". The agent cannot tell a redundant order from an impossible one, and\nthose call for opposite corrections.\n\n## The fix\n\nA `DesignationManager.DesignationOn` / `DesignationAt` pre-check emitting\n`already-designated` as its own reject key. Roughly five lines, and it makes\n`rejects_by_reason.already-designated` a free per-call count of wasted orders —\nwhich is the same ledger goal 4087644's comment #1 argues for on the job side.\n\n## Hazards for whoever takes it, read from source\n\n- **`DesignationOn` and `DesignationAt` each `Log.Error` on a targetType\n  mismatch.** Mine and MineVein are targetType Cell — use\n  `DesignationAt(cell, def)`. Hunt is targetType Thing — use\n  `DesignationOn(thing, def)`. Backwards is a RED ERROR, not a silent null, and\n  a red error breaches the zero-red-errors invariant.\n- **`Designator_Hunt.CanDesignateCell` is not bare — it is actively wrong.** It\n  returns `\"MessageMustDesignateHuntable\"` even when the real cause is\n  already-designated. A wrong reason is worse than a null one: null at least\n  signals absence, while this one sends the reader somewhere else entirely.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- A designate order on an already-designated cell or thing returns\n  `already-designated` as its own reject key, distinct from `not-designatable`.\n- Mine/MineVein route through `DesignationAt`, Hunt through `DesignationOn`, and\n  a test exercises both so a swapped pair fails loudly rather than logging red.\n- The Hunt `CanDesignateCell` wrong-reason case is either corrected or\n  documented at the call site as a known misattribution.\n- Zero red errors across the run.","files":null}]}